---
// 03-CONTENT.md §4. No equivalent section in the template — built in its
// visual language on the hull (dark navy) tone.
---

<section id="vision-mission">
  <div class="diag-divider diag-divider--hull" aria-hidden="true" />
  <div class="container">
    <h1 class="section-heading">Where we are going</h1>

    <div class="row vm-block reveal">
      <div class="col-md-8 col-md-offset-2">
        <p class="vm-label">Vision</p>
        <p class="vm-text vm-lead">
          To be the most trusted operating company in Philippine digital
          entertainment — the one that partners choose because our systems
          hold, our records are clean, and our standards do not move when
          nobody is watching.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row vm-block reveal">
      <div class="col-md-8 col-md-offset-2">
        <p class="vm-label">Mission</p>
        <p class="vm-text">
          We build, run, and support regulated digital entertainment
          platforms to a standard that regulators, partners, and players can
          rely on. We do this by engineering our own technology rather than
          renting it, by developing Filipino talent into specialists in a
          field that has few of them, and by treating regulatory compliance
          and player protection as the foundation of the business rather
          than a cost of doing it. Every system we administer is built to be
          inspected, and every team we run is trained to expect it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  #vision-mission {
    color: #fff;
    text-align: center;
    padding: 6em 0;
  }

  .vm-block {
    margin-top: 56px;
  }

  .vm-label {
    font-family: "Oswald", sans-serif;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.6);
    font-size: 0.9em;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  .vm-text {
    color: #fff;
    font-size: 1.1em;
    line-height: 1.6em;
  }

  .vm-lead {
    font-size: 1.35em;
    line-height: 1.5em;
  }
</style>
